              }

              // THE WALLET ANSWERED WITH NOTHING. wallet_provider.js tags the
              // Wallet Standard rejections that prove a wallet is there and
              // simply authorized no account — a dismissed account-selection
              // sheet, or every account deselected. Opaque, but true; the setup
              // copy would be readable and false.
              if (e && e.walletAnswered) throw e;

              // ── THE WALLET'S OWN WORDS DIE ON THE NEXT LINE, SO THEY ARE
              //    REPORTED ON THIS ONE ────────────────────────────────────────
              //
              // The substitution below is the ONE place in this app that throws
              // away a wallet's error string on purpose, and it is the reason
              // report-client-wallet-failures captured almost nothing for the
              // class it was built for. Downstream, every catch sees only the
              // sentence composed here; parseSolanaError has no rule for it, so
              // it passes through unchanged and the report arrives with
              // `raw_message` and `mapped_message` BYTE-IDENTICAL. The pair is
              // the whole diagnostic value of the call — `raw` is what makes a
              // MIS-mapping visible — and for the 2026-09-06 incident that
              // motivated the reporting work (an empty Phantom, a user told to
              // check their USDC balance seven times) the raw string WAS the
              // mapped string. Only a `4001` decline, rethrown untouched by the
              // guard above, ever carried a genuine wallet string.
              //
              // So the report is made HERE, where `em` still holds what the
              // wallet actually said, rather than at a surface that can only see
              // what we replaced it with. This is the fourth call site named
              // during the original build and deferred then; the three surface
              // call sites stay exactly as they are for every OTHER rejection,
              // which reaches them intact.
              //
              // `mapped` is the sentence the user will read, not a guess at it:
              // this rethrow is the only thing the surface has to work from, and
              // parseSolanaError's pass-through leaving it untouched is pinned by
              // test/views/wallet_connect_error_copy_test.rb. A change that broke
              // that coupling would redden there before it could lie here.
              //
              // FIRE AND FORGET, like every other call site — `typeof` guard,
              // no await, and the reporter swallows its own faults
              // (app/javascript/solana_errors.js). Observation may not delay,
              // block or alter the failure a user is about to be handed.
              var setupCopy = 'Finish setting up your wallet in ' + brand + ' \u2014 create or import one, then try again.';
              if (typeof window.reportWalletFailure === 'function') {
